%I A002009 M5314 N2308 #30 Nov 08 2026 16:46:09
%S A002009 56,1120,18592,300288,4877824,80349696,1344154112,22821564416,
%T A002009 392763133952,6842542866432,120517760139264,2143547238776832,
%U A002009 38461421887881216,695577645926711296,12669549172922908672,232264091566234140672,4283069601827515269120,79406931456918332375040
%N A002009 Number of rooted planar maps with 2n+1 trivalent vertices and a root vertex of valence 7.
%D A002009 R. C. Mullin, E. Nemeth and P. J. Schellenberg, The enumeration of almost cubic maps, pp. 281-295 in Proceedings of the Louisiana Conference on Combinatorics, Graph Theory and Computer Science. Vol. 1, edited R. C. Mullin et al., 1970.
%D A002009 N. J. A. Sloane, A Handbook of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1973 (includes this sequence).
%D A002009 N. J. A. Sloane and Simon Plouffe, The Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1995 (includes this sequence).
%H A002009 Christopher Smolen, <a href="/A002009/b002009.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..200</a>
%H A002009 R. C. Mullin, E. Nemeth and P. J. Schellenberg, <a href="/A002005/a002005.pdf">The enumeration of almost cubic maps</a>, Proc. of the Louisiana Conference on Combinatorics, Graph Theory and Computer Science. Vol. 1, (1970), 291-295 [scanned annotated copy].
%H A002009 Christopher Smolen, <a href="https://github.com/chrispbsmolen/almost-cubic-maps">Almost cubic maps: programs, b-files and three computations of the Mullin-Nemeth-Schellenberg table</a>
%H A002009 Jian Zhou, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.03883">Fat and Thin Emergent Geometries of Hermitian One-Matrix Models</a>, arXiv:1810.03883 [math-ph], 2018.
%F A002009 From _Christopher Smolen_, Nov 07 2026: (Start)
%F A002009 a(n) = A002005(n+3) - 8*A002005(n+2) + 6*A002005(n+1) - 6*Sum_{i=0..n+1} A002005(i)*A002005(n+1-i).
%F A002009 G.f.: (C(x) - 1 - 4*x - 32*x^2)/x^3 - 8*(C(x) - 1 - 4*x)/x^2 + 6*(C(x) - 1)/x - 6*(C(x)^2 - 1)/x, where C(x) is the g.f. of A002005. (End)
%o A002009 (Python)
%o A002009 from math import factorial
%o A002009 def dfact(n):
%o A002009     r = 1
%o A002009     while n > 1: r *= n; n -= 2
%o A002009     return r
%o A002009 def c(n): return 2**(2*n+1)*dfact(3*n)//(factorial(n+2)*dfact(n))  # A002005
%o A002009 def d(n): return sum(c(i)*c(n-i) for i in range(n+1))
%o A002009 def a(n): return c(n+3) - 8*c(n+2) + 6*c(n+1) - 6*d(n+1)  # _Christopher Smolen_, Nov 07 2026
%Y A002009 Cf. A002005, A002006, A002007, A002008, A002010.
%K A002009 nonn,changed
%O A002009 0,1
%A A002009 _N. J. A. Sloane_
%E A002009 Name clarified and a(7)-a(17) from _Christopher Smolen_, Nov 07 2026
